              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log in to Microsoft OneDrive, you can use the direct links and instructions below depending on how you are trying to access it:\n\n### 1. Log in via Web Browser\nIf you are on a computer, tablet, or phone browser:\n*   **Direct Login Link:** Go directly to the **[OneDrive Sign-In Page](https://onedrive.live.com)**.\n*   **Alternative Link:** Go to **[Microsoft 365](https://microsoft365.com)**, sign in, and click the **Apps** icon (the 9 dots in the top-left corner) and select **OneDrive**.\n*   **Steps:** \n    1. Enter your Microsoft email address (e.g., `@outlook.com`, `@hotmail.com`, or your work/school email).\n    2. Enter your password.\n    3. If prompted, complete your two-factor authentication (if enabled).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Log in on Windows (Desktop App)\nOneDrive is built directly into Windows 10 and Windows 11.\n1. Click the **Start** button and type **OneDrive**, then select the app.\n2. If it\u2019s your first time opening it, a setup window will appear. Enter your Microsoft account email address and click **Sign in**.\n3. Enter your password. \n4. Once completed, your OneDrive files will sync directly to your **File Explorer** under a folder named \"OneDrive\".\n\n*(Note: If the app isn't installed, you can search for the gray or blue cloud icon in your taskbar, or download it from the Microsoft Store).*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Log in on Mac (Desktop App)\n1. Open your Mac's **Finder** and go to **Applications**.\n2. Open **OneDrive** (if you don't have it, you can download it from the Mac App Store).\n3. Enter your Microsoft account credentials when prompted to sign in and set up your sync folder.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Log in on Mobile (iPhone, iPad, or Android)\n1. Download the **Microsoft OneDrive** app from the Apple App Store or Google Play Store.\n2. Open the app.\n3. Type in your Microsoft email address and password.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Trouble Logging In?\n* **Forgot Password?** Click the \"Forgot password?\" link on the sign-in page to verify your identity and reset it.\n* **Work or School Account?** If your account was provided by an employer or school, make sure you use your organization's specific email and password. Sometimes, this requires signing in through your organization's portal.",
